WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.741 --> 00:00:06.416
Meet Aperture, your embedded AI consultant team for biopharma strategy.

2
00:00:06.653 --> 00:00:09.984
Work through conversation, as you would brief a colleague.

3
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:11.585
Tell the team what you need,

4
00:00:11.874 --> 00:00:14.476
ask follow-up questions, and guide the work.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.304
Your Chief of Staff turns the conversation into a plan.

6
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:26.247
Here, we explore 4L+ relapsed/refractory multiple myeloma, anchored on elranatamab.

7
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.952
Review the task card,

8
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.367
check the scope, evidence sources, and limits, then approve.

9
00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:35.179
Your dedicated Associate gets to work:

10
00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:39.411
retrieving public records from databases like ClinicalTrials.gov,

11
00:00:39.765 --> 00:00:44.281
or processing and reformatting private inputs you are permitted to use.

12
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:48.605
As tasks are completed, results populate your workspace,

13
00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:53.226
with organized discovery assets and links to the underlying evidence.

14
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.044
Explore the clinical timeline to compare programs and milestones.

15
00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.312
Use the automatically calculated Relevance Index

16
00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:03.187
to focus your next questions.

17
00:01:03.423 --> 00:01:04.671
Then return to chat.

18
00:01:04.895 --> 00:01:08.200
Ask for an explanation, request a deeper comparison,

19
00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:10.153
or direct the next task.

20
00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.650
You lead the strategy.

21
00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:14.866
Your AI team helps move the work forward.

22
00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:18.473
Aperture. Clinical strategy, in focus.
